    <h2>Core Privacy Principle: On-Device Processing &amp; Zero Audio Storage</h2>
    <p><strong>NeuralVox: Lie Detector</strong> ("the App"), developed by independent developer <strong>Gaurav Deore</strong> (operating under <strong>DevPhoton</strong>), is engineered with an uncompromising <strong>privacy-first architecture</strong>.</p>
    
    <div class="highlight-box">
        <p style="margin: 0;"><strong>Summary:</strong> Your voice is never recorded to files, never saved to storage, and never transmitted across the internet. All acoustic measurements (pitch and tremor frequency calculations) are performed live in temporary device memory (RAM) and immediately wiped. We collect zero personal data, and there are zero tracking SDKs.</p>
    </div>

    <h2>1. Microphone Usage &amp; Complete Audio Privacy (<code>RECORD_AUDIO</code>)</h2>
    <p>The App requests access to the device microphone solely to enable the party game's voice stress mechanics:</p>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Volatile Memory Only:</strong> When the Interrogator taps to record a baseline or question response, short audio samples (typically 2 to 4 seconds) are held strictly in temporary RAM buffers for digital signal processing (DSP).</li>
        <li><strong>No Audio Files Created:</strong> The application <strong>never writes audio files</strong> (such as WAV, MP3, or M4A) to your internal storage, external SD card, or cache directories.</li>
        <li><strong>No Cloud Transmission:</strong> Audio data never leaves your device. The App connects to no external voice processing servers, AI cloud backends, or third-party APIs.</li>
        <li><strong>Immediate Erasure:</strong> As soon as the acoustic metrics (average pitch, jitter, and tremor modulation) are calculated, the raw audio buffer in memory is immediately cleared and overwritten.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>2. Information We Do NOT Collect</h2>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>No User Accounts:</strong> You do not need to register, create a profile, or provide an email address, username, or password.</li>
        <li><strong>No Personal Identifiers:</strong> We do not collect names, phone numbers, contact lists, photos, device IMEI, or advertising IDs.</li>
        <li><strong>No Location Tracking:</strong> The App does not request, access, or log GPS coordinates, coarse location, or IP-based location data.</li>
        <li><strong>No Third-Party Analytics SDKs:</strong> The App contains no tracking or telemetry frameworks (no Firebase Analytics, AppsFlyer, Facebook SDK, Adjust, or Google Analytics).</li>
        <li><strong>No Data Brokering:</strong> We do not sell, rent, monetize, or disclose any user data to third parties or advertising brokers under any circumstances.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>3. Data Stored Locally On Your Device</h2>
    <p>The App stores only minimal, non-identifying operational preferences in your device's private local sandbox (Android <code>PlayerPrefs</code>):</p>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>UI Theme State:</strong> Light Mode or Dark Mode preference toggle.</li>
        <li><strong>Audio Volume Preferences:</strong> In-game sound effect volume toggles.</li>
        <li><strong>Question Deck Selection:</strong> Your active question deck choice (e.g., Icebreakers, Spicy, Custom).</li>
    </ul>
    <p>This data never leaves your device and is not accessible to other applications.</p>

    <h2>4. Android Permissions &amp; Hardware Access</h2>
    <p>NeuralVox requests only the minimum permissions required to deliver its core party game experience:</p>
    <ul>
        <li><strong><code>android.permission.RECORD_AUDIO</code>:</strong> Required to capture live vocal input during the calibration and interrogation phases. Used exclusively for on-device real-time math analysis in volatile RAM.</li>
        <li><strong><code>android.permission.VIBRATE</code>:</strong> Optional permission used to deliver subtle tactile haptic feedback during countdowns, button presses, and verdict reveals.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>5. Google Play Services &amp; Store Ingestion</h2>
    <p>App distribution, installation binaries, and automated updates are handled directly by Google Play under the standard <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Privacy Policy</a>. DevPhoton does not manage or maintain separate user accounts for store distribution.</p>

    <h2>6. Data Retention, Portability &amp; Deletion</h2>
    <p>Because NeuralVox operates offline and stores only local settings on your phone, you have total control over all app data:</p>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Complete Deletion:</strong> You can permanently wipe all local settings at any time by going to:
            <br>
            <code>Settings &gt; Apps &gt; NeuralVox &gt; Storage &gt; Clear Storage / Clear Data</code>
        </li>
        <li><strong>Uninstallation:</strong> Uninstalling the application immediately and irreversibly removes all local sandbox files and cached preferences.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>7. Children’s Privacy (COPPA &amp; GDPR Compliance)</h2>
    <p>NeuralVox is designed as a party game suitable for general audiences. Because the App collects no personally identifiable information (PII), creates no persistent audio recordings, and uses no third-party behavioral trackers, it is fully compliant with the Children's Online Privacy Protection Act (COPPA), the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR), and Google Play's Families Policy.</p>

